From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:22:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] re-anchor position:fixed rect queries by the viewport scroll

The fixed-position hoist re-parents fixed boxes into the root element's
layout children, which paint_scene translates by -viewport_scroll; so
'fixed' boxes scrolled away with the page. The hoist shipped documenting
the caveat ('correct at scroll 0'), but interactive sessions scroll
routinely, and a fixed compact header vanished as soon as the page
scrolled.

Maintain the invariant 'fixed location = taffy location +
viewport_scroll' (apply_fixed_scroll_anchor, tracked by
fixed_anchor_scroll): resolve() re-bakes it right after taffy resets
locations, and set_viewport_scroll applies incremental deltas so
scroll writes re-anchor immediately; static pages may never resolve
again, and rect queries / hit tests read layout locations between
paints. Layout positions are what paint, hit-testing, and rect
queries all consume, so one adjustment keeps every consumer
viewport-pinned.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: fixed boxes are now laid out by Taffy
against the viewport, and upstream cancels the root and viewport scroll
for them in paint (hoisted_child_position) and hit-testing. Baking the
scroll into layout locations as well would cancel it twice, so the
location re-anchoring is dropped and only rect queries
(physical_unrounded_geometry, behind getBoundingClientRect) get the same
cancellation, which upstream lacks.
---
 src/document.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index 2e2a82c..b31882a 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -2999,6 +2999,22 @@ impl BaseDocument {
             pos.x += node.unrounded_layout().location.x - node.scroll_offset().x as f32;
             pos.y += node.unrounded_layout().location.y - node.scroll_offset().y as f32;
             current = node.containing_block();
+            // A fixed box contained by the root element is positioned against
+            // the viewport and does not scroll with it: cancel the root and viewport
+            // scroll the walk (and the caller's viewport-relative conversion) applies,
+            // as paint and hit-testing do (`hoisted_child_position`). Otherwise
+            // getBoundingClientRect on a fixed header drifts up by the page scroll.
+            if node.taffy_position() == taffy::Position::Fixed
+                && let Some(cb) = current.and_then(|cb| self.nodes.get(cb))
+                && cb
+                    .containing_block()
+                    .and_then(|id| self.nodes.get(id))
+                    .is_none_or(|parent| matches!(parent.data, NodeData::Document(_)))
+            {
+                let viewport_scroll = self.viewport_scroll();
+                pos.x += cb.scroll_offset().x as f32 + viewport_scroll.x as f32;
+                pos.y += cb.scroll_offset().y as f32 + viewport_scroll.y as f32;
+            }
         }
         (pos, *self.nodes[node_id].unrounded_layout())
     }
